    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (82.99) and **Brice Turang** (73.39), who represent the engine of our SB-focused strategy. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Michael King; while King\u2019s moderate hold rate slightly tempers expectations, the elite projected score remains the highest on the roster due to his multi-category ceiling. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns a massive boost from a projected leadoff slot and his ability to exploit Bubba Chandler\u2019s slow delivery, which maximizes his stolen base equity. **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) also stands out as a strong play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Shane Bieber (xERA 5.48) and a platoon advantage that keeps his floor high in the Roto standings.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was finding the correct threshold for **Jose Caballero** (54.15). While he occupies a marginal spot due to an unfavorable platoon matchup against a right-handed arm, his role as a speed specialist keeps him in the mix. **Dalton Rushing** (40.12) is the most precarious start of the day; his L/L platoon disadvantage against Matthew Boyd and a drop to the #9 spot significantly suppress his score, leaving him barely above our benching threshold. We continue to monitor the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** as potential depth, but none currently offer a better daily efficiency profile than the starters listed.\n\nRegarding our bench, the absence of **Josh Naylor**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Austin Riley**, and the injured **Vinnie Pasquantino** leaves us thin, but our current utility options\u2014specifically **James Wood** (65.15)\u2014justify the roster construction. **James Wood** remains a high-value play despite facing a tough arm in Aaron Nola, as his elite xwOBA of 0.422 provides enough raw offensive talent to overcome the matchup risk. All managers should note that we are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters; if **Dalton Rushing** is pushed further down the order or scratched, we will look to rotate our bench depth to preserve our precious game caps. **Mickey Moniak** (52.75) warrants careful watching as well, as his platoon disadvantage against Ian Seymour creates a high variance outcome that could drag on our team AVG if he doesn't capitalize on his park-adjusted power.",
